pocket-ui @VERSION@: install from the card's PC-readable partition (Retroid Pocket Mini V2)
==========================================================================================

No SSH, no Wi-Fi, no command line. You flash the official ROCKNIX image, copy two files onto the card
from your PC, and start the device twice. pocket-ui is not made or endorsed by the ROCKNIX team.

You need
--------

- A Retroid Pocket Mini V2 and a microSD card, and a PC or Mac with a card reader.
- The official ROCKNIX image for SM8250, version @TESTED_ROCKNIX@ (the tested one), from rocknix.org.
  Flash it to the card as ROCKNIX describes, and set the device up to boot it as ROCKNIX describes.
- These two files from the zip: mount-storage.sh and pocket-ui-seed.tar.gz.

Install
-------

1. Flash the ROCKNIX image to the card. Do NOT start the device with it yet.
2. Take the card out and in again so your PC shows it. It shows ONE drive, called ROCKNIX (the other
   partitions are Linux ones and stay invisible; that is normal).
3. Copy mount-storage.sh and pocket-ui-seed.tar.gz into the top folder of that drive. Do not rename them,
   do not unpack the .tar.gz. Eject the card safely.
4. Put the card in the device and switch it on. First start: ROCKNIX grows its storage to the size of
   the card and restarts by itself. It looks like a normal ROCKNIX start. Wait.
5. Second start: you see "pocket-ui: installing", then pocket-ui opens with its first-start setup.
   The two files vanish from the drive by themselves. You are done.

It also works on a card that already runs ROCKNIX (copy the two files, switch the device on; it installs
at that start). About @NEED_MB@ MB free are needed. Your games, saves and settings are never touched;
the installer only adds files.

If it did not work
------------------

ROCKNIX always starts (with EmulationStation) even when the install fails, and the reason is written
into the file pocket-ui-install.log on the same drive. Read it on your PC. Typical reasons:
- "damaged": the tar did not copy completely. Copy it again.
- "not grown": ROCKNIX did not enlarge its storage. Flash the card again and copy the files before the first start.
Both files stay on the card until the install worked, so you can fix the cause and start again.
Without the log: you copied the files to the wrong partition (the drive must be the ROCKNIX one).

To remove pocket-ui later: open an SSH session to the device (ROCKNIX: root / rocknix) and run
  sh /storage/pocket-ui/uninstall.sh
EmulationStation is back after the next start.

Built from commit @REPO_COMMIT@.
